se_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129486" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "The product is undefined"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129486" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\times 7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n$Y=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$U=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of $YU?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that $Y$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $U$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $Y$ and $3$ rows in $U.$ Since the number of columns in $Y$ equals the number of rows in $U,$ the matrices $Y$ and $U$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $YU$ has dimensions $1\\times 1:$\n\n$$\n{Y}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{U}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}={YU}_{1\\times 1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9257f8c40add6ab1b82355accdf9587b7750c84fd830461d2b204bd0b61c3bd" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1\\times 1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1\\times 3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\times 1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\times 3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "The product is undefined"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/state.json" "file_sha256" "83bde52d19ee01cda00814b9fad01cc00ece6f9617075c72eacf4b36df781aa7" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4403.json" "file_sha256" "25df0447da85d2d9cfe7903748737ca8c58ea38ab3dca22bb8c0d02d539e5aa4" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4403.json" "file_sha256" "25df0447da85d2d9cfe7903748737ca8c58ea38ab3dca22bb8c0d02d539e5aa4" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $A$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $AB$?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4404.json" "file_sha256" "ba40b60282c7702de045ff3bd76c567ea63daeb81dd2284c44223e8aeea09ccc" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4404.json" "file_sha256" "ba40b60282c7702de045ff3bd76c567ea63daeb81dd2284c44223e8aeea09ccc" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4405.json" "file_sha256" "06a6a75f0633306bcd63df9227f33f6386016125bce8ffb3ab7207da4dd18d7b" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/example-4405.json" "file_sha256" "06a6a75f0633306bcd63df9227f33f6386016125bce8ffb3ab7207da4dd18d7b" "basis" 918 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979047/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-22056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $R,S,$ and $T?$\n\n- The product $SR$ is well defined\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $ST$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $T$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $T.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $T,$ the matrices $S$ and $T$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "19da14c480c1696049b4ec1dc163b75c3514799072d232300b8774a3b2343a82"} {"question" "q-22056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\n- The product $AB$ is well defined\n- The product $BA$ is well defined\n- The product $AC$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that all three statements are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "19da14c480c1696049b4ec1dc163b75c3514799072d232300b8774a3b2343a82"} {"question" "q-42374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,K=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,L=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $J,K,$ and $L?$\n\n- The product $JK$ is well defined\n- The product $KL$ is well defined\n- The product $JL$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $J$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $L$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $J$ and $3$ rows in $K.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $K,$ the matrices $J$ and $K$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{K}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $K$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $K$ equals the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $K$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{K}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $J$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $J$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement II is true, while statements I and III are false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "19da14c480c1696049b4ec1dc163b75c3514799072d232300b8774a3b2343a82"} {"question" "q-42375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42375" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42376" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $D,E,$ and $F?$\n\n- The product $ED$ is well defined\n- The product $FD$ is well defined\n- The product $EF$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42376" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $E$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $F$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $E$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $F$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $F$ and $D$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{D}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-42376" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1