 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{3\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "19da14c480c1696049b4ec1dc163b75c3514799072d232300b8774a3b2343a82"} {"question" "q-22063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22063" "field" "selection" "at