"value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-320351" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-320351" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={BA}_{2\\times 2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "19da14c480c1696049b4ec1dc163b75c3514799072d232300b8774a3b2343a82"} {"question" "q-22067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\times 2"] ["math" "2\\times 4"] ["math" "4\\times 2"] ["math" "4\\times 4"] ["text" "The product is undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "q-22067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\times 2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/state.json" "file_sha256" "51f682884bb9c5defb70dd7fa5b0eb1b81ba1972bffb25410de7fe90f70cb0b0"} {"question" "e-4403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/5357fcb0ec150699b4d50cbd6fa9651c421ac3500660703396146362160328a2.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/63d354773d145f05e73e808efe2a21164cb28d6ff19ae104d6bbde6510cf10e6.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/example-4403.json" "file_sha256" "214448cb950029f06798f7c9a4c48b52cd071250657b31724761851deca71be7"} {"question" "e-4403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/example-4403.json" "file_sha256" "214448cb950029f06798f7c9a4c48b52cd071250657b31724761851deca71be7"} {"question" "e-4404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose $A$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $AB$?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/example-4404.json" "file_sha256" "ad27a416d2177500ad1ddd973dcd98ec09b7554eb507d31be3d4bc967e61f743"} {"question" "e-4404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/example-4404.json" "file_sha256" "ad27a416d2177500ad1ddd973dcd98ec09b7554eb507d31be3d4bc967e61f743"} {"question" "e-4405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/035755bae569c8c9323112891f959076dd727d3ef40ba66c6c40dadf5ddc8f84.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/e53c9ba3bb64b81e44f8f4f49ac77408b7db6ee458be3d43b687d9ed8897ad59.png)\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/example-4405.json" "file_sha256" "35ea473fc871a50f387209440f6c426a172eb5da64217498e8e6e19410a256d1"} {"question" "e-4405" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/example-4405.json" "file_sha256" "35ea473fc871a50f387209440f6c426a172eb5da64217498e8e6e19410a256d1"}] "usage" {"q-129486" [] "e-4403" [] "q-22067" [] "e-4404" [] "q-42374" [] "q-22063" [] "e-4405" [] "q-77475" []} "basis" 1607 "retractions" [[17592186101317 :question/problem "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$,\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A, B$, and $C$?\n\n1. The product $AB$ is well defined\n2. The product $BA$ is well defined\n3. The product $AC$ is well defined"] [17592186101235 :question/problem "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A, B$, and $C$?\n\n1. The product $AB$ is well defined\n2. The product $BA$ is well defined\n3. The product $AC$ is well defined"] [17592186101237 :question/problem "Let\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA$?"] [17592186101237 :question/answer-fields 17592186099159] [17592186100604 :question/problem "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{ali